# Accepted exceptions to the image Gate (job image-gate in
# .github/workflows/pr.yml). Trivy skips every vulnerability ID listed here,
# one per line.
#
# This file is empty on purpose: every HIGH or CRITICAL finding blocks the PR
# until it is fixed. Fixing means a dependency or base image update, not an
# entry here.
#
# An entry is added only when a finding cannot be fixed yet, and only with a
# comment directly above it that gives both:
#   1. the justification: why it cannot be fixed now, for example no fixed
#      version exists yet, or the fix needs a breaking upgrade;
#   2. the reason it is safe: why the vulnerable code cannot be reached or
#      exploited in this image.
# An entry without both is not merged. Remove the entry in the PR that ships
# the fix.
#
# Format (example, not a real entry):
#   # CVE-2099-0001 in example-lib 1.2.3. Justification: no fixed version yet.
#   # Safe because: the app never calls the vulnerable parser.
#   CVE-2099-0001
